IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), s 204 (Part 6, Division 1): the director's offences and their penalties.
-- Each offence has a "guilty" function (the elements) and the penalty is one function over the offence and whether it was committed with intent to defraud.
-- Whether the director "fails to comply with section 201(2) or (5)" is the answer of the section 201 modules; here it is the fact the offence starts from.
-- A penalty record gives the highest fine, the longest imprisonment (0 months where the text gives none), whether the Court may impose both, and whether a default penalty also applies.

DECLARE `s 204 offence` IS ONE OF
    `s 204(1) failing to comply with section 201(2) or (5)`
    `s 204(1AA) failing to comply with section 201(16)`
    `s 204(1A) the failure in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)`

DECLARE `s 204 penalty` HAS
    `s 204 the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 204 the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `s 204 the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 204 a default penalty also applies` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Section 204(1): section 201(2) or (5)`

-- src:18995 | 204.—(1) If any director of a company fails to comply with
-- src:18996 | section 201(2) or (5), he or she shall be guilty of an offence and shall
-- src:18997 | be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $250,000.
@ref s 204(1) (src:18995-18997)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director fails to comply with section 201(2) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(1) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director of the company` AND `the director fails to comply with section 201(2) or (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If any director of a company fails to comply with section 201(2) or (5), he or she shall be guilty of an offence" (an unmet element of the offence: the provision's own question, fork F-S1 of NOTES.md)

§ `Section 204(1AA): section 201(16)`

-- src:19003 | (1AA) If any director of a company fails to comply with
-- src:19004 | section 201(16), he or she shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:19005 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000.
@ref s 204(1AA) (src:19003-19005)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director fails to comply with section 201(16)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(1AA) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director of the company` AND `the director fails to comply with section 201(16)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If any director of a company fails to comply with section 201(16), he or she shall be guilty of an offence" (an unmet element of the offence: the provision's own question, fork F-S1 of NOTES.md)

§ `Section 204(1A): the other provisions of the Division`

-- src:19009 | (1A) If any director of a company —
-- src:19011 | (a) fails to comply with any provision of this Division (other
-- src:19012 | than section 201(2), (5) or (16));
-- src:19017 | (b) fails to take all reasonable steps to secure compliance by
-- src:19018 | the company with any such provision; or
-- src:19020 | (c) has by his or her own wilful act been the cause of any
-- src:19021 | default by the company of any such provision,
-- src:19023 | he or she shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction
-- src:19024 | to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:19025 | exceeding 2 years.
@ref s 204(1A) (src:19009-19025)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision concerned is section 201(2), (5) or (16)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director fails to comply with a provision of this Division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director fails to take all reasonable steps to secure compliance by the company with such a provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director has by his or her own wilful act been the cause of any default by the company of such a provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(1A) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF    `the person is a director of the company`
       AND (NOT `the provision concerned is section 201(2), (5) or (16)`)
       AND (   `the director fails to comply with a provision of this Division`
            OR `the director fails to take all reasonable steps to secure compliance by the company with such a provision`
            OR `the director has by his or her own wilful act been the cause of any default by the company of such a provision`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If any director of a company — (a) fails to comply with any provision of this Division (other than section 201(2), (5) or (16)); (b) fails to take all reasonable steps to secure compliance by the company with any such provision; or (c) has by his or her own wilful act been the cause of any default by the company of any such provision, he or she shall be guilty of an offence" (an unmet element of the offence: the provision's own question, fork F-S1 of NOTES.md; "(other than X)" is one of the six left to the encoder: a failure of section 201(2), (5) or (16) is for subsections (1) and (1AA), so this subsection answers JUST FALSE for it; the other reading is NOTHING)

§ `Section 204(2): the defence for an omission`

-- src:19029 | (2) In any proceedings against a person for failure to take all
-- src:19030 | reasonable steps to comply with, or to secure compliance with, the
-- src:19031 | preceding provisions of this Division relating to the form and content
-- src:19032 | of the financial statements of a company or consolidated financial
-- src:19033 | statements of a parent company by reason of an omission from the
-- src:19034 | financial statements or consolidated financial statements, it is a
-- src:19035 | defence to prove that the omission was not intentional and that the
-- src:19036 | information omitted was immaterial and did not affect the giving of a
-- src:19037 | true and fair view of the matters required by section 201 to be dealt
-- src:19038 | with in the financial statements or consolidated financial statements.
@ref s 204(2) (src:19029-19038)
GIVEN `the proceedings are for failure to take all reasonable steps to comply with, or to secure compliance with, the provisions of this Division on the form and content of the statements by reason of an omission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the omission was not intentional` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information omitted was immaterial and did not affect the giving of a true and fair view of the matters required by section 201 to be dealt with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(2) the subsection gives the person a defence on these facts` MEANS
    IF NOT `the proceedings are for failure to take all reasonable steps to comply with, or to secure compliance with, the provisions of this Division on the form and content of the statements by reason of an omission`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the defence is for "any proceedings against a person for failure to take all reasonable steps ... by reason of an omission from the financial statements", and the subsection is silent on any other proceedings (a scope limit with no "only": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))
    ELSE IF `the omission was not intentional` AND `the information omitted was immaterial and did not affect the giving of a true and fair view of the matters required by section 201 to be dealt with`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is a defence to prove that the omission was not intentional and that the information omitted was immaterial and did not affect the giving of a true and fair view" (the defence ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b): when it is not proved, "this section gives no defence on these facts")

§ `Section 204(3): intent to defraud`

-- src:18995 | 204.—(1) If any director of a company fails to comply with
-- src:18996 | section 201(2) or (5), he or she shall be guilty of an offence and shall
-- src:18997 | be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $250,000.
-- src:19003 | (1AA) If any director of a company fails to comply with
-- src:19004 | section 201(16), he or she shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:19005 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000.
-- src:19023 | he or she shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction
-- src:19024 | to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:19025 | exceeding 2 years.
-- src:19042 | (3) If an offence under this section is committed with intent to
-- src:19043 | defraud creditors of the company or creditors of any other person or
-- src:19044 | for a fraudulent purpose, the offender shall be liable on conviction —
-- src:19046 | (a) in the case of an offence under subsection (1), to a fine not
-- src:19047 | exceeding $250,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:19048 | exceeding 3 years or to both;
-- src:19052 | (aa) in the case of an offence under subsection (1AA), to a fine
-- src:19053 | not exceeding $100,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:19054 | exceeding 3 years or to both; or
-- src:19058 | (b) in the case of an offence under subsection (1A), to a fine
-- src:19059 | not exceeding $15,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:19060 | exceeding 3 years or to both.
@ref s 204(1), (1AA), (1A) and (3) (src:18995-19060)
GIVEN offence IS A `s 204 offence`
      `the person is guilty of an offence under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is committed with intent to defraud creditors of the company or creditors of any other person or for a fraudulent purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 204 penalty`
`s 204 the most the offender may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under this section`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalties are those of "an offence under this section"; where the person is not guilty of one the section fixes no penalty
    ELSE IF `the offence is committed with intent to defraud creditors of the company or creditors of any other person or for a fraudulent purpose`
         THEN (CONSIDER offence
               WHEN `s 204(1) failing to comply with section 201(2) or (5)` THEN JUST (`s 204 penalty` OF 250000, 36, TRUE, FALSE)
               WHEN `s 204(1AA) failing to comply with section 201(16)` THEN JUST (`s 204 penalty` OF 100000, 36, TRUE, FALSE)
               WHEN `s 204(1A) the failure in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` THEN JUST (`s 204 penalty` OF 15000, 36, TRUE, FALSE))
         ELSE (CONSIDER offence
               WHEN `s 204(1) failing to comply with section 201(2) or (5)` THEN JUST (`s 204 penalty` OF 250000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)
               WHEN `s 204(1AA) failing to comply with section 201(16)` THEN JUST (`s 204 penalty` OF 50000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)
               WHEN `s 204(1A) the failure in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` THEN JUST (`s 204 penalty` OF 10000, 24, FALSE, FALSE))

§ `Section 204(4): imprisonment only for a wilful offence`

-- src:19062 | (4) A person shall not be sentenced to imprisonment for any offence
-- src:19063 | under this section unless in the opinion of the Court dealing with the
-- src:19064 | case the offence was committed wilfully.
@ref s 204(4) (src:19062-19064)
GIVEN `the offence is one under section 204` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the Court dealing with the case the offence was committed wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(4) the person is barred from being sentenced to imprisonment for the offence` MEANS
    IF NOT `the offence is one under section 204`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on imprisonment "for any offence under this section", and the subsection is silent on any other offence (a scope limit with no "only": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))
    ELSE IF `in the opinion of the Court dealing with the case the offence was committed wilfully`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person shall not be sentenced to imprisonment for any offence under this section unless in the opinion of the Court dealing with the case the offence was committed wilfully" (a bar closed by "unless": the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 2; the "unless" once met is one of the six left to the encoder, the other reading is NOTHING)
         ELSE JUST TRUE
